WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.840
Connecting DesignaKnit to your Brother

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:09.130
electronic machine is a matter
of connecting the BL1 or the BL5 cable

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:13.530
between the machine and your
computer with DAK installed.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.450
The USB cable has three parts.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.170
The USB end connects to a USB
port on your computer.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.170
The square end with the small
prongs connects to the machine.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.360
On the 930, 940, remove the small plastic

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.090
cover to reveal the port
on the back of the machine.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:40.570
On the 970, the port is on the CB1 box.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:46.610
With the two ends now connected,
the computer can now talk to the machine.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:52.050
Next, position the black box,
and I'm sure there's a better name for it,

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.970
on the body of the machine
near the row counter.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.320
Position it with the red dot facing

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.370
the front of the machine
and the cable tables towards the back.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.080
Use Velcro to attach this so you can

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:09.530
easily remove it to use
it with other machines.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:15.010
Finally, position the Knitlink
magnet arm to the K-carriage.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.960
Position it so it passes
in front of the black box.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:26.530
On the 970, be sure that the arm
clears the manual row counter.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.890
As you pass the magnet,
a red light will blink and a will be sent

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:36.250
to DesignaKnit to record that you've
passed the carriage and you've knit a row.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.600
You need to let DesignaKnit know what

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:43.090
machine you're using and connect
the computer to DesignaKnit.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.650
I'm in Standard Garment Styling
and from the menu, I'll choose >Options,

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.960
click >Method of Knitting,

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.680
then choose >Machine, and click >OK.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:06.440
Click the >Setup button and then

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:14.570
click >Find Link and >start search.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.570
DesignaKnit will connect to your
computer to set things up.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.010
A message will display when
the connection is made.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.680
Click >OK.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.720
Scroll to choose your
machine and then click >OK.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.200
With everything in place,

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:36.530
your machine and DesignaKnit will
be able to talk to each other.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.320
In interactive Knitting,
the magnet will let DesignaKnit know you've

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:44.920
knit a row, and DesignaKnit will give
you your knitting instructions.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:50.640
In Stitch Designer, this setup will allow
you to download stitch patterns to your

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:56.770
machine or upload built-in stitch patterns
to DesignaKnit so that you can modify them.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.890
If you'd like to learn more about using

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.600
DesignaKnit , please visit learnDesignaKnit.
Com.

